{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25256 - PROTEIN:4299",
  "verbalization": "Specionin is implicated in the targeting of Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Specionin acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Cytochrome c4, 6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin, and (2E,6E)-3,7,11-Trimethyl-9-(phenylsulfonyl)-2,6,10-dodecatrien-1-ol, all of which are known to interact with the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits. This indicates a potential mechanism where Specionin may function as a modulator or ligand that influences the activity of these ATPase subunits. The shared target of these compounds suggests a possible functional relationship, where Specionin could either directly interact with the ATPase subunits or influence their activity through a common pathway. The evidence supports the idea that Specionin may play a role in the regulation of these transporters, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
